<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amawari</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1458</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amawari was lord of Katsuren Castle on Okinawa in the mid-fifteenth century and a powerful rival of the Ryukyuan royal court. In 1458 he persuaded King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-taikyu">Shō Taikyū</a> that his rival <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gosamaru">Gosamaru</a> was planning rebellion, and Gosamaru was destroyed. When Amawari then moved against Shuri himself, royal forces defeated and killed him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amawari.jpg" alt="Amawari" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kugel~commonswiki · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tomb_of_Amawari.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
